    <item>
      <title>含时演化的歌</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/songs/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 03 Mar 2026 00:36:00 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/songs/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;　　生活快步向前，心境含时演化。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;　　含时演化算符是量子力学中描述量子态随时间变化的算符，这个算符好像也作用在我身上。发现自己总会在一段时间突然爱上一首歌，或是恰恰契合当时的心境，或是为旋律折服。每每听到这些歌时，与之串联的记忆会止不住地涌上心头。&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>科学是一场建模</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/science-is-a-grand-enterprise-of-modeling/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 26 Feb 2026 18:49:00 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/science-is-a-grand-enterprise-of-modeling/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;　　近期在先前量子力学的基础上学习分子谱学，深感震撼。我想科学理论从来不是无限逼近绝对真理的线性过程，而是一套基于实证、可证伪、可迭代的拟合模型。科学的进步，是一场 “建模 - 检验 - 修正 - 重构” 的螺旋式上升过程，这也许是科学区别于空想的核心。&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>What Did Hubble See on Your Birthday?</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/what-did-hubble-see-on-your-birthday/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Feb 2026 17:24:00 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/what-did-hubble-see-on-your-birthday/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;alt&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/posts/what-did-hubble-see-on-your-birthday/figures/hubble.jpg&#34;&gt;
The Hubble Space Telescope captured this image on my birthday in a certain year. The star-forming region, called Sharpless 2-106, looks like a celestial angel. The &amp;ldquo;wings&amp;rdquo; of the nebula are twin lobes of hot gas that stretch outward from a massive, young star near the center of the image. In this boundless cosmos, what was going through my mind back then?&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
